# Code owners (feat-5-foundation-monorepo-ci, REQ-007, DEC cc4449cd-78fb-452a-904f-7efda89cf004).
#
# A change to these paths needs the review of the owner. A coding agent must
# not be able to switch off a gate, so the list has the files that start,
# configure or check the gates.
#
# The entry for the thresholds is added when the walking skeleton makes them.
# Branch protection must have "Require review from Code Owners" (Task 130.150).

# The decisions
/docs/dec/            @dfch

# The CI configuration, and this file
/.github/workflows/   @dfch
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @dfch

# The entry point of all gates
/justfile             @dfch

# The version pins, the gate scripts and the list of licenses
/tools/               @dfch

# The model of the architecture (the DSL, the one file a person edits, and the generated JSON;
# feat-50-structurizr-model-rules, Task 160.120). The model is the source of the architecture rules (DEC
# b6e8808f-86b4-41a4-92f2-33d38869beed, the DSL is the source; DEC e85e9685-0787-4dff-9ee5-9d46670e9ee4, the
# conventions): a change of the model changes the rules that stop the build (the recipes architecture-backend,
# architecture-frontend and architecture-model, and the gate check-model-generated), so the owner reviews it.
/model/               @dfch

# The allowlist of the secret scan (gitleaks). The folder /tools/ covers it already. This line says on purpose that a
# change of the allowlist, which hides a finding, needs the review of the owner (feat-8-traceability-security-gates).
/tools/security/gitleaks.toml   @dfch
